      "area": "curl scale and shoulder placement",
      "finding": "The improved R090 construction is expanded in the cel. Its top return spreads underneath the chin over the far collar. The next fronts mask much more of the far white shoulder ruffle and outer red bow, and the tail now reaches the top of the waistband. The visibly full reference R090 preserves a slimmer shoulder-edge run, with a smaller curl relative to its head; a head-width adjustment cannot explain the growth from v11. This is an artwork relationship, outside a whole-character camera translation or scale correction."
    }
  ],
  "P2": [],
  "observations": [
    "The native front bands read as two large turns, one separate narrower turn, then C. The three visible opaque dark gray inner folds read continuously, match the relative tone family of the original R090, and fall within the current dark-gray tolerance. Mint reads as a narrow stripe. There is real air inside C and around parts of the lower ribbon.",
    "The false opaque white slots from v11 have been replaced with real gray hair folds. The remaining tiny white frill below the second turn is part of the wardrobe. Under-jaw anchor remains on the intended viewer-right anatomical LEFT and the sleeve/bow overlap places the curl in front; concealed bead/anchor geometry cannot be certified.",
    "Two open uneven eyes, closed smile, cap leaves, compact bob, near elbow and cuff at waist, black-red-white costume and crossed shoes remain recognizable in the original pose. F895 is the tighter skirt-crop and canonical full-body guide F2374 preserves both shoes. Both QA images match direct alpha composites of the exact raw."
  ],
